1919,r795ya,Xaggitin XL 54mg,"[""Xaggitin XL 54mg""]",True,negative,"[""I've had ADHD since I was 5 yrs old (am 28 now) and all the previous medications I have been on have not affected my sleeping patterns, although my parents were told that they would (lies as usual lol)\n\nWas on methylphenidate hydrochloride 10mg 4x a day from the age  17 till I was  25 when (for reasons I won't go into here) the mental health nurse/Dr put me on concerta 36 mg once a day, and still didn't get any disruption to my sleeping patterns. \n\nIn July 2021(4 months ago) Dr changed my meds to Xaggitin XL 5g once a day, to which my sleeping patterns went all to f**k! \n\nI used to be able to go to bed at 10pm and sleep till 9am but I was also able to go to bed at 2 or 3am and still get up at 9am, BUT NOW if I try going to bed at even just 11pm I cannot for the life of me fall asleep and it's getting later and later that I finally manage to get to sleep!\nPast 3 weeks it's been 7 or 8am when I've finally nodded off and I slept till 5pm!""]",author,True,clearly attributed negative effect on sleep patterns
2025,r6h98l,Strattera,"[""Strattera""]",False,neutral,"[""Started Strattera. Anyone tried it before?""]",author,False,Author reports side effects but does not express clear positive or negative sentiment toward the drug. No explicit evaluation of benefit or harm.
2025,r6h98l,Adderall,"[""Adderall""]",False,negative,"[""I’ve abused adderall and vyvanse years back but remember when i took them before abusing the adderall made my head feel clear and like everything wasn’t overlapping anymore. I could hear my own thoughts and had less trouble with emotional dis regulation. I didn’t really like vyvanse. I was a mean person on it and always felt sick.""]",author,False,"Author describes positive effects from Adderall (clarity, emotional regulation) but also negative effects (being 'a mean person', feeling sick). However, the context is framed as past abuse, not current use, and the author does not express a preference for or against Adderall in the present. Sentiment is mixed but not clearly attributed to the drug in the context of current use. For this post, we treat the sentiment as negative due to the author’s explicit negative description of the drug’s effect on them during abuse, which is not the current context. However, this is ambiguous and may not reflect current sentiment. We flag as negative for now, but this is uncertain."
