2029,r6gbrq,Adderall,"[""Adderall""]",False,neutral,"[""So I've been on Adderall for 15 years (as well as other psych meds)""]",author,False,No explicit sentiment expressed about Adderall; author states it's been working for them but does not evaluate it positively or negatively.
2142,r5mnu1,Strattera,"[""Strattera""]",False,negative,"[""I did my research and found that Strattera is not typically used as a first line drug and that it has chemical similarities to antidepressants (I had harsh side effects while starting and stopping SSRIs years ago). I also read studies saying it doesn’t work in the majority of ADHD patients, particularly when they are primarily inattentive (as I am). This seemed like an obvious instance of risks outweighing potential benefits, so I elected not to take it and made an appointment with a second psychiatrist.""]",author,False,"explicitly named, clear negative sentiment, author's own evaluation"
2142,r5mnu1,Wellbutrin,"[""Wellbutrin""]",False,negative,"[""I explained my concerns about Strattera and the first doctor but she said Wellbutrin was different. I did a few minutes of research and found, once again, that Wellbutrin is not a first line drug for ADHD and that it is an antidepressant with many of the same side effects.""]",author,False,"explicitly named, clear negative sentiment, author's own evaluation"
