3123,qx7yzg,Ritalin,"[""Ritalin""]",False,mixed,"[""I was prescribed concerta before starting college but I did not like how it made me feel. It definitely helped me concentrate but the come down was awful. I told my doctor this and Instead was prescribed Ritalin which I like 100x better."", ""I now take 2 pills a day (spaced out with at least 4 hours in between a dose) which is fine but I’ve noticed I’ve been taking it only because it puts me in a good mood and makes me more outgoing. I can use it to be productive, but instead I use it to feel happy and play good during video games. Now I just look forward to taking my medication so I can feel good.""]",author,False,"Author explicitly states preference for Ritalin over Concerta, but also describes use for mood enhancement and recreational purposes, indicating mixed sentiment."
3131,qx4wcu,Ritalin,"[""Ritalin""]",False,neutral,"[""I’m female, 20. Psychiatrist recently told me I have ‘symptoms of ADHD’ and is letting me try Ritalin.""]",author,False,"Author reports side effects and questions whether they will resolve, but does not explicitly label the drug as positive, negative, or mixed. No clear evaluation of benefit or harm is stated."
