3798,qs5e1g,modafinil,"[""modafinil""]",False,positive,"[""I was diagnosed with ADHD (combined type) with Major Depression last year. \n\nPre-diagnosis, I took modafinil as needed because it helped me stay laser focused and work long hours.""]",author,False,explicitly stated benefit for focus and productivity
3798,qs5e1g,concerta,"[""concerta""]",False,mixed,"[""After a few weeks, I told her I couldn’t feel the difference. So she prescribed me 36mg concerta, and the first few times taking it I felt an adrenaline-like rush in my body. \n\n(Similar to modafinil’s effect) \n\nSo I told her, it was working. \n\nFast forward to a year, I had a depressive relapse, and I stopped ADHD meds for a month since I couldn’t afford it. \n\nAnd, weird thing is, I could actually focus at work that time. I told this to my psychiatrist and started doubting if concerta was even working for me. \n\n(Plus, I’ve now pinpointed my nausea, heartburn, acid reflux, and bloatedness to concerta) \n\nShe agreed that we could test a lower dose. \n\nI tried 3 days no meds. Then 3 days with concerta 18mg. I felt stomach sick within those 3 days that I couldn’t be productive at all. \n\nSo I tried taking modafinil again, and, so far…\n\nI seem to be performing better on modafinil vs. concerta.""]",author,False,"initially reported benefit (adrenaline-like rush), later reported lack of benefit (focus issues during relapse) and negative side effects (nausea, acid reflux, bloatedness, inability to be productive)"
