8107,q76u6p,Xanax,"[""Xanax""]",True,mixed,"[""I've been on some Xanax like medication for the past 10 days, but those we're temporary. I still have some more, but the doctor told me that it's addictive and that it wont work longterm... I want to take them, because it calms me down... but on the other hand, he said it was more like, if it got really bad and i ended up in bed again? But it's really bad, all day, every day... And i want to lie in bed, I can't find the energy to go for a walk, meditate or a tiny workout.""]",author,True,Author expresses both desire to use for relief and concern over addiction and short-term efficacy; sentiment is mixed.
8107,q76u6p,Zoloft,"[""Zoloft""]",False,negative,"[""I'm on 150mg Zoloft, I've been on it for like 2 months or so now. I've been on it for a long period of time earlier, and it helped then, but back then it was combined with mirtaszapine and abilify. Now it doesn't do anything, in fact - I'm wondering if its making it worse?""]",author,False,Author explicitly states the medication is ineffective and questions whether it is worsening symptoms.
