9166,nthnlm,Sertaline,"[""Sertaline""]",True,mixed,"[""I’ve been receiving therapy from my college. My therapist is amazing although unfortunately short term. I’m undiagnosed with PTSD. It’s gotten a lot worse lately I see things that aren’t there auditory and visual. One of the psychiatrists put me on sertaline an SSRI it’s the genetic form of Zoloft. I’m more than lactose intolerant, I’ve discovered that having any dairy product even medicines is really scary. A couple years ago I lost a lot of weight from a medicine that had casein protein in it (derived from milk) While taking sertaline I’ve lost 2 Ibs-4Ibs! I don’t really have much more weight I can lose. I’m supposed to slowly wean myself off sertaline. I don’t know if I have another 4 Ibs to lose. I’m definitely getting pretty scared especially after my last experience with weight loss it was horrible I got so sick.""]",author,True,"Mixed sentiment: author reports weight loss (possibly beneficial) but also fear and discomfort from the side effect, and is scared of the medication's effects. Sentiment is not clearly positive or negative."
